    "description": "<p><strong>Sigil</strong></p><h3>Seal</h3><p>Make a <strong>Power Roll</strong> against a creature or device within Very Close range. On a success, a short memory or a piece of data is temporarily erased.</p><p>The GM can <strong>spend a Fear</strong> to let the forgotten memory or information resurface.</p><p><strong>Seal:</strong> After you successfully use this card, you can <strong>mark a Hit Point</strong> to flip it to its <strong>Release</strong> side.</p><h3>Release</h3><p>Make a <strong>Power Roll</strong> against a creature or device within Very Close range. On a success, their identity or data are temporarily erased. If the target is an adversary, they cannot use any of their features. If the target is a device, it temporarily stops functioning.</p><p>The GM can <strong>spend 2 Fear</strong> to let the lost identity or data resurface.</p><p><strong>Release:</strong> After you use this card, flip it back to its <strong>Seal</strong> side.</p>",
